{
  "activity_uuid": "activity_28fe9636-519a-5fb4-ab4a-eab53491098d",
  "name": "2.1 Perimeter of basic plane figures",
  "activity_type": "TYPE_DYNAMIC",
  "activity_sub_type": "SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE",
  "content": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Perimeter of basic plane figures"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Learning objective: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Calculate perimeter and recover missing lengths in squares, rectangles and triangles."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Understand the concept"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Perimeter is the total length of the boundary of a closed figure. A square with side s has perimeter 4s. A rectangle with length l and breadth b has perimeter 2(l + b). For any triangle, add its three side lengths; for an equilateral triangle this is 3s."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Convert all lengths to the same unit before adding. Perimeter uses linear units such as cm or m, not square units."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "blockMathEquation",
        "attrs": {
          "math_equation": "P_{\\mathrm{square}}=4s,\\qquad P_{\\mathrm{rectangle}}=2(l+b)"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Worked examples"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example 1: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A rectangular garden is 13 m long and 8 m wide. Find its perimeter."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solution: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "2(13 + 8) = 42 m."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example 2: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "An isosceles triangle has perimeter 35 cm and equal sides of 12 cm. Find the base."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solution: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "35 − 12 − 12 = 11 cm."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Independent practice"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work these out in your notebook before looking at the self-check below."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "1. ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Find the perimeter of a square of side 9 cm."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "2. ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A rectangle has perimeter 58 m and length 19 m. Find its breadth."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Self-check"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Compare your method and answer. If you are unsure, revisit the relevant worked example before taking the chapter checkpoint."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "1. ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "36 cm."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "2. ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "58 ÷ 2 − 19 = 10 m."
          }
        ]
      },
